From cc39dfd0c46302fddf52c7484840666b2e5d6fb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:19:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 109/116] MAS local: the volume button brings up Android's
 volume panel

The title bar's volume button opened a bar of its own under itself, as
MuMu has it. It now brings up Android's own volume panel instead, as a
volume key does: a click runs `cmd media_session volume --show --stream 3
--adj same` over adb, which shows the system's panel for the media
stream and leaves the volume where it is. The shell's own cmd
media_session is turned down by AppOps on API 34, so the command runs
through `su 0` first and falls back to the plain shell where there is
no su. adb runs on the AdbInterface's own thread, so the window does not
wait for it.

When the button is shown (only while the emulator plays sound), its tool
tip, and its being disabled without the manager's adb server or without
adb, are unchanged.

Gone with the bar: LeanVolumePopup, reading and parsing the volume, the
one at a time sender, the unmute index, where the bar opens on the
screen, the title bar's buttonsDisabled signal, the muted speaker icon,
and their tests.

Test: aemu-ui-lean-window_unittests (44), android-emu-adb-interface_unittests
(26). On flow-a (API 34) `su 0 cmd media_session volume --show --stream 3
--adj same` brings up VolumeDialogImpl and keeps the volume.

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#226

